course: dictionary
lesson: 4746
title: Horseshoe: one word, two shapes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A horseshoe is a U-shaped piece of metal nailed under a horse's hoof to protect it. The word can also mean anything shaped like a U, so you need the context to know which meaning is meant.
explain: «A blacksmith fits one horseshoe on each hoof, so every horse needs 4 horseshoes.» The clues are blacksmith, hoof and horse, so here horseshoe means the metal shoe.
explain: «The greater horseshoe bat has a nose leaf shaped like a horseshoe.» The clue is shaped like, so here horseshoe means the U shape. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A horseshoe can mean a U-shaped piece of metal nailed to a horse's hoof.
fact: A horseshoe can also mean anything shaped like a U, such as a horseshoe magnet or a horseshoe bend in a river.
fact: «Horseshoe» is a noun. One is a horseshoe, and more than one is horseshoes.
fact: «Horseshoe-shaped» describes something that curves round like a U.
fact: Many people hang a horseshoe over a door because it is a sign of good luck.
exercise: «A blacksmith fits one horseshoe on each hoof, so every horse needs 4 horseshoes.» How many horseshoes does one horse need? | 2 | 8 | 1 | *4
exercise: Mia says a horseshoe magnet must be a magnet shaped like a horse's shoe. What does horseshoe mean in a horseshoe magnet? | *Anything shaped like a U | A loud noise | A soft, woolly sock | A horse's metal shoe
exercise: «6 horses, of which 2 already have shoes: 6 − 2 = 4 horses still need shoes, and 4 × 4 = 16 horseshoes.» How many horseshoes are needed for the 4 horses that still need shoes? | *16 | 12 | 4 | 24
test: «A horse chestnut leaf leaves a horseshoe-shaped scar on the twig.» What does horseshoe-shaped mean here? | Long and straight | *Curved like a U | Round like a ball | A hard metal shoe
test: A river can have a horseshoe bend. What does horseshoe bend mean? | *A bend shaped like a U | A fish that swims in shallow water | A fast, straight stream | A bridge made of metal
exam: «Here a line of great white pelicans swims forward in a horseshoe, drives fish into shallow water, then all the heads dip at once.» What does horseshoe mean here? | A metal shoe on a bird's foot | *A curved U-shape formed by the birds | A sandy beach | A kind of fish
